-- examples/checks/not-as-a-name.rofl — A PROGRAM THAT MUST BE REFUSED.
--
-- `not(1).` is a fact about a relation called `not`, and for a while the
-- TypeScript parser took it — `literal()` read the name and asked no questions,
-- so the reading of `not` depended on whether an `(` or an identifier followed
-- it, one token apart. The Rust parser refused it at `relbook`. Both refuse it
-- now, and the golden holds that they do.
--
-- The complement is examples/checks/keyword-atom.rofl: the same word in
-- argument position is a word, and both hosts load it.

not(1).
